The AI provider and its model
administrator-20-the-ai-helper
One provider and one model serve every account. The check box marks the provider in use; none marked means the AI is off. Anthropic, OpenAI, Google and DeepSeek come with their connection details and a default model filled in: you supply the key. Custom is the fifth choice, where you fill in everything yourself, the model included.
S opens the setup dialog for the provider under the cursor. It looks the same every time: the Key, the Model and Other name. The key is a password field: what you type or paste is shown as *, and when a key is already set the field shows a row of stars that keeps it. The Model is a list of the provider's own model names, with the one in use chosen. With no key yet, enter the key and press Tab: the key goes to the AI helper and the list is filled from the provider with it. Other name is only for a model the list does not hold, such as on a Custom server that gives no list. Save sets what you chose. Model names are case-sensitive: a model set with the wrong capitals is pointed out and the listed one chosen.
The key is kept by the AI helper (the service account NT SERVICE\sd-ai, encrypted for that account) and sent only to the provider's address over https, with the certificate checked. It goes to the helper through a file only SDSYS can reach, which is removed at once; it is never on a command line or in the audit trail. To keep a key out of SD altogether, type it at the helper's own prompt instead: set.ai key PROVIDER. On Windows SDSYS is an elevated Administrator and can read the key, as any Windows administrator of this machine can.
Selecting a provider means that the text accounts send leaves this machine for that provider. An account can send text only if its ai gate is on (the Accounts box). Nothing is on as delivered: no provider, no key and no account.
Enter selects or deselects the provider. S sets it up (key and model), X clears the key, C fills in Custom, D removes it, A sets the file of certificate authorities for a private CA, L changes a limit. At the prompt: set.ai.
T opens the standing text: a few lines sent first with every AI request from every account, telling the AI what SD is and where its help is. SD ships a default; edit it and choose Save to send your own, or Shipped default to go back. It is invisible to a person asking the AI and does not change their question. A text that names SD's own code is refused.
